# <Project> Function Book

Check this book and the code before writing a new function. Reuse a listed function when it fits. Extend one when it nearly fits, without breaking its current callers. Add a new entry when you create a shared function.

The book lists only what other code is meant to call: shared helpers, value-object factories, domain policies, persistence and security helpers, and API extensions. It does not list handlers or private methods.

## How to use an entry

| Field | Meaning |
| --- | --- |
| Function | Signature as callers see it |
| Location | File path from the component root |
| Purpose | What it does and the business rule it carries |
| Parameters / returns | Meaning of each input; what success and failure look like |
| Use when / notes | When to call it, when not to, known limits |

